.Dd 2025-12-25
.Dt DARKMAN 1
.Os
.Sh "نام (NAME)"
.Nm darkman
.Nd control dark-mode and light-mode transitions
.Sh "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Ar command
.Sh "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.Nm
runs in the background and turns on dark mode at sundown, and turns it off
again at sunrise.
.Nm
is not designed to be used interactively: it's designed to be set up once,
and run in the background.
.Pp
It is also possible to trigger manual transitions and it is also possible to
disable automatic transitions entirely.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm run Op Fl -ready-fd Ar fd
Runs the
.Nm
service.
This command is intended to be executed by a service manager, init script or
alike.
.Pp
The optional
.Ar fd
is a file descriptor where
.Nm
will notify when it is ready to receive connections from clients.
The protocol used is compatible with readiness notifications for s6, dinit
and systemd.
.It Cm set Aq Cm light | dark
Sets the current mode.
.It Cm get
Prints the current mode.
.It Cm toggle
Toggle the current mode.
.El
.Sh "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -verbose
Print detailed logs.
Defaults to
.Cm true
for the
.Cm run
command and to
.Cm false
for all other commands.
.El
.Sh "پیکربندی (CONFIGURATION)"
See
.Xr darkman.conf 5
for configuration file format and
.Sx FILES
for configuration file locations.
.Sh INTEGRATIONS
The open source desktop ecosystem is quite heterogeneous and making different
applications switch between dark/light requires different mechanisms.
.Pp
.Nm
seeks to implement the more widely adopted standards, while leaving room
for users to hook in custom scripts for other applications.
.Ss Custom executables
.Nm
can run custom executables (which can be simple shell scripts).
.Pp
Scripts are searched in a directory named
.Pa darkman
inside paths defined in the
.Ev XDG_DATA_DIRS
as well as
.Ev XDG_DATA_HOME .
Each script receives the current mode
.Pq Dq dark No or Dq light
as its first argument ($1).
This allows a single script to handle both modes:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#!/bin/sh
case "$1" in
dark) THEME=dark-theme ;;
light) THEME=light-theme ;;
esac
gsettings set org.example.app theme "$THEME"
.Ed
.Pp
For backwards compatibility,
.Nm
also searches
.Pa dark-mode.d
and
.Pa light-mode.d
directories (legacy format).
Scripts in these directories run without arguments.
Scripts in the
.Pa darkman
directory with the same name will override legacy scripts.
.Pp
Both of these variables and their fallbacks are defined in the XDG Base
Directory Specification:
.Lk https://specifications.freedesktop.org/basedir-spec/latest/
.Pp
These scripts or executables can perform any actions required like re-write
configuration files for a PDF reader, control a notification daemon to
switch to another theme, or toggle a DE-specific setting.
.Pp
Files must have the executable bit set in order to be considered an executable.
Scripts must have the proper shebang for the OS to properly execute them.
.Pp
Typically, the
.Ev XDG_DATA_*
variables mentioned above will resolve to the following set of directories:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.Pa ~/.local/share/
.It
.Pa /usr/local/share/
.It
.Pa /usr/share/
.El
.Pp
Example scripts (and discussion on how to integrate different applications) are
available in the project repository:
.Lk https://gitlab.com/WhyNotHugo/darkman
.Pp
Packages may also drop-in their own scripts into any of these locations,
although application developers are encouraged to use the socket API to
determine the current mode and listen for changes (see below for details).
.Ss XDG Settings portal
.Nm
implements the XDG desktop portal's dark mode interface.
Applications using this API should switch to dark/light mode based on
.Nm Ns 's
current preference.
This interface was originally pushed by the GNOME and Elementary teams, and is
currently supported by KDE, Firefox and many other projects.
You should expect applications from those environments to support it, amongst
others.
.Pp
For more details on this protocol, see:
.Lk https://flatpak.github.io/xdg-desktop-portal/docs/doc-org.freedesktop.portal.Settings.html
.Pp
As of
.Xr xdg-desktop-portal 1
version 1.17.0, portals MUST be configured with per-user configuration
.Xr portals.conf 5 .
To force the usage of
.Nm
for dark/light mode setting, use something like the following:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[preferred]
org.freedesktop.impl.portal.Settings=darkman
.Ed
.Pp
When using a desktop-specific configuration (e.g.:
.Pa swaywm-portals.conf ) ,
please keep in mind that the environment variable
.Ev XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP
must be set for the
.Xr xdg-desktop-portal 1 .
.Pp
The
.Xr xdg-desktop-portal 1
should start after
.Nm
has started and is ready.
Use
.Fl -ready-fd
for readiness notification.
This is likely not relevant on systemd-based setups, where the service manager
intermediates in taking the named bus.
.Pp
For a more in-depth explanation, see this article:
.Lk https://whynothugo.nl/journal/2024/04/09/darkman-portal-configuration/
.Ss Socket API
.Nm
listens on a Unix socket for query and control commands.
The socket exposes a simple text-based API where commands are followed by a
newline, and
.Nm
writes a response also followed by a newline.
.Pp
The
.Cm get , set
and
.Cm toggle
commands use this API.
It is also the recommended approach when writing custom tools
(e.g.: switching the current mode based on the input from a light sensor).
.Pp
The following commands are available:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm get
Print the current mode.
.It Cm set Ar mode
Set the current mode.
.Ar mode
must be one of
.Cm light
or
.Cm dark .
.It Cm toggle
Switch to the opposite mode.
The new mode is printed as a response.
.It Cm watch
Print mode changes as they occur.
The current mode is printed immediately, followed by each subsequent change.
.El
.Pp
To interact with the socket manually:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
socat UNIX-CONNECT:${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR}/darkman/control.sock STDIO
.Ed
.Pp
A
.Nm libdarkman
Go package is available to query this interface from other client applications.
See its documentation for details:
.Lk https://godocs.io/gitlab.com/WhyNotHugo/darkman/libdarkman
.Ss Third party integrations
For Emacs users, a third party package exists to integrate
.Nm
with Emacs:
.Lk https://github.com/grtcdr/darkman.el
.Pp
There also exists a plugin for neovim users:
.Lk https://github.com/4e554c4c/darkman.nvim
.Sh LOCATION
The current location may be specified in the configuration file.
The location is used to calculate what time sundown and sunrise happen.
.Pp
It is also possible for
.Nm
to automatically determine the system's location using
.Xr geoclue 1 .
Geoclue's reliability varies depending on distribution and desktop environment,
as an agent often needs to be configured for it to work properly.
.Pp
If no location is known, automatic transitions are disabled.
.Sh "محیط (ENVIRONMENT)"
The following environment variables are also read and will override the
configuration file:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev DARKMAN_LAT
Overrides the latitude for the current location.
.It Ev DARKMAN_LNG
Overrides the longitude for the current location.
.It Ev XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP
.Nm
does not use this variable; it should be defined for the
.Xr xdg-desktop-portal 1
instead.
.El
.Sh "فایل‌ها (FILES)"
.Nm
searches for a configuration file in the following locations, using the first
one found:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/darkman/config.yaml
.It
Each directory in
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_DIRS ,
with
.Pa darkman/config.yaml
appended.
.El
.Pp
If
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is not set, it defaults to
.Pa ~/.config .
If
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_DIRS
is not set, it defaults to
.Pa /etc/xdg .
.Pp
See
.Xr darkman.conf 5
for configuration file format.
.Sh PRIVACY
.Nm
will trigger a darkmode/lightmode transition at sundown in the current
location.
Any application that is running locally can record or transmit the time of
these transitions and attempt to extrapolate information related to the current
location.
.Pp
When a web browser applies this transition at the same time, open websites can
record this information too.
.Pp
A potential stalker or tracker can use the above information to infer that you
are likely in a region of the world where sunset happened at a specific time.
This region is usually a wide area spanning tens of thousands of kilometers, but
can be smaller for certain geographical locations.
.Pp
The author of this tool uses a manually configured location with an integer
latitude and longitude to achieve a sensible balance between privacy and
convenience.
.Sh DEVELOPMENT
For issues and general development inquiries, see the project home currently
hosted at GitLab:
.Lk https://gitlab.com/WhyNotHugo/darkman
.Sh DEBUGGING
To confirm which value is relayed via the
.Xr xdg-desktop-portal 1
use:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gdbus call --session \e
    --dest org.freedesktop.portal.Desktop \e
    --object-path /org/freedesktop/portal/desktop \e
    --method org.freedesktop.portal.Settings.ReadOne \e
    org.freedesktop.appearance color-scheme
.Ed
.Sh "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.Xr portals.conf 5 ,
.Xr gammastep 1 ,
.Xr sd-ready-fd 1
